 Every `user` includes a `suspended` boolean. Suspension revokes existing sessions, prevents signing in, and unassigns the user's tickets. Restoring access does not restore the old sessions or assignments. An admin cannot suspend the last active admin.
 
+## Staff groups
+
+Groups organize tickets but do not restrict access: admins and agents can browse all groups, memberships, and tickets in their account. Only admins can change groups and memberships.
+
+| Method and path | JSON body | Success |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `GET /groups` | — | `200` with `groups` |
+| `GET /groups/:id` | — | `200` with `group` |
+| `POST /groups` | `{"group":{"name":"Billing"}}` | `201` with `group` |
+| `PATCH /groups/:id` | `{"group":{"name":"Invoices"}}` | `200` with `group` |
+| `DELETE /groups/:id` | — | `204` |
+| `GET /group_memberships` | — | `200` with `group_memberships` |
+| `GET /group_memberships/:id` | — | `200` with `group_membership` |
+| `POST /group_memberships` | `{"group_membership":{"group_id":20,"user_id":12,"default":true}}` | `201` with `group_membership` |
+| `PUT /group_memberships/:id/make_default` | — | `200` with `group_membership` |
+| `DELETE /group_memberships/:id` | — | `204` |
+
+Both lists are ordered by ascending `id`. The membership list supports `group_id` and `user_id` filters. Staff can belong to multiple groups, with one membership per group. The first membership becomes the default automatically; use `default: true` on creation or `make_default` to change it. When a default membership is deleted, the remaining membership with the lowest ID becomes the default. Suspension preserves memberships and defaults.
+
